  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Considering API Key Strategy**\n\nI\'ve decided to prioritize graceful fallback for Gemini endpoints since the user opted out of the paid API key setup. That means I need to ensure all requested functionalities work with the free tier key, likely falling back to `gemini-3.8-flash` where necessary. It\'s a key consideration.\n\n\n**Refining Access Control**\n\nI\'m now focusing on a robust verification plan, specifically for access control and role switching. I need to ensure that the application correctly handles transitions between roles like OWNER, ADMIN, and RECEPTIONIST. I\'m detailing specific accessible features for each role, with particular emphasis on preventing unauthorized access to financial data for non-administrative roles, as per ultra-mode requirements.\n\n\n**Developing Reservation Features**\n\nI\'m currently focused on implementing new reservation input with automatic OTA commission calculation and OTA syncing. I\'m building out a system for selecting rooms, dates, booking channels, and seeing the calculations for revenue, commission, and net profit. The system will handle the OTA sync and monthly P&L updates. I am considering the ADMIN or OWNER role for expense entries, and the impact to monthly reports.\n\n\n**Designing Financial Displays**\n\nI am now structuring the Profit & Loss Statement and designing essential screens. I\'m building an Executive Dashboard with KPIs like Occupancy Rate and Net Profit, a Kalender & Status Kamar view for room management, and a Reservasi & Channel Manager for bookings. In addition, I am implementing a Rate Plan & Komisi OTA section, and finally, a Biaya (Expenses) section is also under development.\n\n\n**Constructing Monthly Reports**\n\nI\'m now fully immersed in developing the automated monthly financial reports, focusing on the Profit & Loss Statement. I\'m structuring it with income by channel, detailed operational expenses across seven categories (including asset depreciation), and a comprehensive final summary. I\'ll include key performance indicators, plus OTA revenue comparisons in a graph. I\'m also preparing for PDF, CSV export functionalities, and, of course, the AI Revenue Advisor.\n\n\n**Mapping Room Details**\n\nI am now carefully mapping the room structure to ensure accurate application of features. I have compared the prompt\'s room descriptions with the details and photos from Hotel Putri Sari. I\'m focusing on aligning the prompt\'s `15 Kamar` structure (5 Deluxe, 5 Standard AC, 5 Economy Fan) with the descriptions, identifying potential discrepancies, and accurately applying room features. I\'ll need to double check the user\'s uploaded data.\n\n\n**Integrating Room Data**\n\nI\'m now integrating the provided room structure and rate plan data, ensuring both descriptions are accurately represented. My goal is to create a seamless system where each of the 15 rooms can be categorized by both Rate Plan Tier (e.g., \"Standard Room\") and Physical Room Subtype (e.g., \"Standard AC\"). I plan to include a one-click preset switcher in the \"Rate Plan & Struktur Kamar\" section, allowing the user to toggle between preset room configurations and pricing. Specifically, I\'m working with a default preset, including 8 Standard, 5 Deluxe, and 2 Family Suites, with associated pricing.\n\n\n"
