  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Crafting File Structures**\n\nI\'m now focused on the application\'s file structures. I need to design and create all the required files, starting with ensuring proper Firebase integration. I\'m starting with `/firebase-blueprint.json` which must adhere strictly to the provided schema. I\'ll need to then create `/security_spec.md` with detailed specifications, focusing on data invariants and other security-related points.\n\n\n**Designing Firestore Schema**\n\nI\'m now focusing on designing the Firestore schema. I\'ve begun modeling the collections under user/property ownership to ensure rule compliance. The `/rooms/{roomId}` collection structure is taking shape, with fields like `ownerId`, `roomNumber`, `name`, `type`, and `physicalCategory` being defined. I am striving for the Eight Pillars of Hardened Rules. Next, I need to design the other collections and their respective fields.\n\n\n**Defining Reservation Schema**\n\nI\'m now deep in defining the `/reservations/{reservationId}` structure. Fields like `ownerId`, `bookingCode`, and `guestName` are taking shape, ensuring they align with the system\'s needs. I\'m focusing on revenue details like `grossRevenue`, `commissionRate`, and `netRevenue`, alongside status options: `Confirmed`, `Checked-In`, `Checked-Out`, and `Cancelled`. I\'m also including `channel` as an enum to track booking source.\n\n\n**Structuring Expense Entries**\n\nI\'m now focusing on the `/expenses/{expenseId}` structure, defining key fields and constraints. I\'m ensuring `ownerId` matches the authenticated user and I\'ve specified an enum for `category` values. Additionally, I\'ve added a date field and `monthKey` for aggregation, alongside creation and update timestamps. My attention is now shifting to the `/settings/{settingId}` structure.\n\n\n"
