  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Constructing Full Architecture**\n\nOkay, the deployment rules are done. I\'m now setting up the full architecture. I\'m modifying `package.json` with `replace_file_content` to configure the `dev` and `start` scripts. This sets up the Express backend and Vite middleware to run on port 3000.\n\n\n**Defining API Endpoints**\n\nI\'m now focused on defining the API endpoints within `/server.ts`. I\'m setting up Express routes for various Gemini API capabilities. I\'ll need to define routes that use specific models like `gemini-4-argon` (with fallback to `gemini-3.8-flash`) for financial audits, `gemini-3.1-flash-lite` for quick receptionist responses, `gemini-3.8-flash` with Google Maps tools, and `gemini-nano-banana-2.1` for image generation (with a fallback as well). Each endpoint will have specific model configurations.\n\n\n**Implementing Image Generation**\n\nI\'m now integrating image generation capabilities. Specifically, I\'m working on generating marketing banners and room photos based on text prompts, potentially using a base64 room photo from the Hotel Putri Sari\'s gallery as a starting point. I\'m focusing on the integration of these features now.\n\n\\n\\n\n\n**Separating Business Logic**\n\nI\'ve decoupled the pure business logic into `/src/utils/hotelCalculations.ts`. I\'m creating extensive unit tests using `node:test` and `node:assert/strict` in `/src/utils/hotelCalculations.test.ts` and also `/firestore.rules.test.ts`. This involves implementing functions to calculate stay breakdowns (weekday vs. weekend rates, all-day flat rates), OTA financials (commission calculations), and monthly profit/loss reports. The `calculateStayBreakdown` function computes the nights and gross revenue while accurately categorizing weekday vs weekend rates. The `calculateOtaFinancials` function computes commission details and the `netRevenue`. I\'m now implementing the calculation of Bagian A (Pendapatan per kamar) within the `generateMonthlyProfitLoss` function.\n\n\n**Calculating Monthly Profit/Loss**\n\nI\'m now implementing the detailed profit and loss calculations within `generateMonthlyProfitLoss`. I\'m working through the components: Bagian A (room revenue and booking channel breakdowns), Bagian B (operational expenses in seven categories), and Bagian C (the final summary with occupancy rate, net profit, and profit margin). This involves calculating metrics like `roomNights`, `grossRevenue`, `commissionRate`, and `netRevenue` for each booking channel.\n\n\n**Defining Key Metrics**\n\nI\'m now focusing on defining key financial metrics within the profit and loss report. I\'m calculating average daily rate (ADR) as well as revenue per available room (RevPAR). I\'ve also incorporated a check for zero net revenue to avoid division by zero errors. I\'m also now implementing an RBAC permission guard called `canRoleAccessView` which restricts roles according to their associated views.\n\n\n"
