  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Reviewing UI Design**\n\nAll unit and security rule tests are passing, which is excellent news. My focus has shifted to the `frontend-design` rules, specifically `references/3_saas_dashboard.md` and `SKILL.md`. I\'m meticulously reviewing the UI design, paying close attention to typography, and verifying that the design is extraordinary and follows all visual rules, starting with the use of `Plus Jakarta Sans`.\n\n\n**Configuring Tabular Typography**\n\nI\'ve specified `IBM Plex Mono` with tabular numerals for key data presentation. I\'m also configuring print styles in `/src/index.css`. The design now mandates clean, unboxed text for static metadata, avoiding rounded pills, and using clean button styles for interactive controls. I\'m actively avoiding anti-patterns like thick borders, pulse animations, and nested cards. High-density data grids will feature right-aligned tabular numerals.\n\n\n**Defining Dashboard Components**\n\nI\'m now focusing on defining the modular components under `/src/components/` for the executive dashboard. I\'ve started outlining `/src/components/ExecutiveDashboard.tsx` and `/src/components/RoomCalendarAndHousekeeping.tsx`, detailing the KPIs, room distribution visualization, channel performance bar charts, room status summaries, reservation tables, and an interactive 15-room grid calendar. I\'m prioritizing data visualization and user interaction.\n\n\n**Detailing Room Data**\n\nI\'m now detailing each of the fifteen rooms, each shown with authentic photos, room numbers, configurations, rates, guest information, cleaning timestamps, and housekeeping buttons. I\'m also including a 14-day occupancy chart and a photo gallery drawer. Furthermore, I\'m integrating a 6-OTA channel connection status bar with a \"Sync OTA Availability\" button and real-time progress indicators.\n\n\n**Implementing Reservation Form**\n\nI\'m now implementing the \"Input Reservasi Baru\" form, complete with automatic calculations for night counts, gross revenue, OTA commissions, and net room revenue based on check-in/check-out dates. I\'m also building a reservations table with filtering, search, and quick actions for check-in, check-out, and cancellation. Check-out automatically sets room status to \"Dirty.\"\n\n\n\n**Adding Expense Input**\n\nI\'m now implementing the `/src/components/OperationalExpensesView.tsx` component, focusing on the expense input form. I\'m building it with 7 mandatory categories: staff wages, utilities, housekeeping, F&B costs, maintenance, marketing, and asset depreciation. This will provide breakdowns with a detailed ledger and filterable by month and year.\n\n\n**Constructing Final Summaries**\n\nI\'m now implementing the executive summary components and accounting data. I\'m focusing on three key sections: the channel performance table detailing revenue and commissions; a detailed expense breakdown with seven categories; and a comprehensive final summary box. I\'m calculating Net Profit and Net Profit Margin, along with Occupancy Rate. I\'m also planning a comparative OTA revenue graph.\n\n\n**Integrating AI & Maps**\n\nI\'m now integrating the requested Gemini features within `/src/components/AiAndMapsHub.tsx`. I\'m structuring a Hospitality Intelligence & Front-Desk Workspace with four tabs: a Revenue & P&L Advisor, a Receptionist Assistant, a Location Guide with Google Maps, and a Room Photo Studio. I\'ll update `/src/index.css` before component creation.\n\n\n"
